
### 4.2 Behind a reverse proxy

Terminate TLS at a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, HAProxy, Traefik). Two
requirements:

1. Forward the `Host` header so the app can build absolute URLs. Set
   `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` to the external https URL; the app prefers it over
   a derived value.
2. Forward `X-Forwarded-Proto` and `X-Forwarded-For`. The audited IP in the
   audit log comes from `X-Forwarded-For` when the proxy sets it; when it
   does not, the audit log records the proxy's address and the operator
   loses the distinction between the proxy and the original caller.

